1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:09,950
You'd moved the bag away. He was cuffed. Could he reach it while you were holding him?

2
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,660
No.

3
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:29,900
We were getting ready to move him. I didn't know what was in that bag.

4
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:36,030
Did he move toward it before your partner opened it?

5
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:38,490
He didn't move.

6
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:47,280
Had your partner checked his ID before opening the bag?

7
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:53,930
Yes. We had grounds to arrest him before we opened it.

8
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:08,480
We logged his property back at the station. That's when we took out the gun and the notebook.

9
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:25,480
The restaurant search was not justified by an immediate threat. The items recovered in that search are excluded.

10
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:43,430
Certain unwarned answers after custody are excluded as well. The remaining evidence requires a separate ruling.

11
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:59,330
The station inventory was lawful. The gun and the notebook remain admissible.

12
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:02,310
That includes these pages?

13
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:07,920
Yes. Those were recovered legally. Don't cross them out.

14
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:18,900
Look at these dates. You'd already decided before Lena sent that message. They'll use that.

15
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:35,850
She offered an appeal form. She didn't send me there. Don't blame her.

16
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:52,330
I won't. But these are still evidence. You need to read them.

17
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:55,310
Leave me the copy.

18
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:58,290
The copy stays here?

19
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:05,990
Yes. Mark what you want to ask me. Don't rewrite what you sent.

20
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:16,380
My mom took today off. Can you call her before she sees the news?

21
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:20,940
I will. Take your time with it.

22
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,800
Put the document's words here. Your own notes on that side.

23
00:03:37,450 --> 00:03:39,780
I've mixed them up.

24
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:59,950
The file says the appeal was incomplete. 'No one read it.' That's my line. I added that.

25
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:19,430
The clinic lists a file that's missing here. Maybe these are different versions. Can Kevin check?

26
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:25,560
He can ask for the records. We don't know yet.

27
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:29,590
If he finds it was sent?

28
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:41,380
Then that's what the records say. It still won't tell us who saw it.

29
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:46,990
Can I send him this? Without the patient names.

30
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:51,550
Yes. Leave my theory out of it.
